%erg 0.1
Title: Downgrade format version from v1 to 0.1 with MAJOR.MINOR scheme
Created: 2026-05-12
Author: user

--- log ---
2026-05-12T12:00Z user created

--- body ---
## Context

The magic line `%erg v1` implies a stable, released format. The format is
still evolving (header set changed post-deployment, Tag renamed, etc.).
Following common magic-line conventions (PDF `%PDF-1.7`, YAML `%YAML 1.2`),
pre-1.0 signals instability and MAJOR.MINOR (no `v` prefix) is standard.

## Actions

1. **Magic line**: `%erg v1` becomes `%erg 0.1`.
2. **Version scheme**: adopt MAJOR.MINOR (two components, no patch).
   Minor bumps add features backward-compatibly; major bump = breaking.
   Pre-1.0 means format may still have breaking minor bumps.
3. **Code changes**:
   - `ergspecv1.go`: rename `magicLine` constant to `%erg 0.1`.
   - `erg.go` (parser): accept `%erg 0.1` as the valid magic line.
     Recognize `%erg v1` as legacy and emit a migration hint.
   - `migrate.go`: extend `migrateFile` to rewrite `%erg v1` first
     lines to `%erg 0.1`. Idempotent, same pattern as Status/Tags.
   - `validate.go` help text: update references.
4. **Doc changes**: update magic line references in `spec-erg-v1.md`,
   `pep-erg-v1.md`, `docs/erg-manual.md`, `README.md`,
   `src/go/assets/spec-erg-v1.md`, `src/go/assets/AGENTS.md`.
   Rename spec/pep files if the naming convention changes.
5. **Corpus migration**: `erg migrate tickets/` rewrites all 140+ `.erg`
   files. One commit for the tooling, one for the corpus rewrite.

## Test

- `erg validate` accepts `%erg 0.1` files, rejects `%erg v1`.
- `erg migrate` rewrites `%erg v1` to `%erg 0.1` idempotently.
- `erg new` creates files with `%erg 0.1` magic line.
- Existing integration tests updated to use new magic line.

## Exit criteria

- No occurrence of `%erg v1` as a live magic line in code or docs
  (quoted references in rationale/history sections are fine).
- `erg migrate` handles v1-to-0.1 rewrite alongside existing Status/Tags rules.
- Spec and PEP document the MAJOR.MINOR versioning convention.
